	quest.1A0E416F2160D2D9.quest_desc: ["&6It is used to whitelist or blacklist specific items, allowing precise sorting into connected chests.&r It offers up to 9 slots for items (stackable), supports NBT matching (configurable), and can be used in either the Inventory Cable Connector or the Basic Inventory Hopper to manage storage."]
	quest.1A0E416F2160D2D9.quest_subtitle: "Read Description"
	quest.1A0E416F2160D2D9.title: "&6You Should Try This&r"
	quest.1A6859592E0984D7.quest_desc: [
		"&bInterfaces&r act like a &6small chest&r and fluid tank that fills itself from and &6empties to network storage&r depending on what you set it to keep a stock of in its slots. "
		""
		"It tries to complete this in a &6single gametick&r, so it can fill itself with or empty itself from up to &69 stacks per gametick&r, making it a fast method of import or export if you have fast item &6pipes&r."
		""
		"Another useful trait is that while most fluid tanks can &6only store 1 type of fluid&r, interfaces can store up to 9, as well as items. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6They're essentially just chests/multi-fluid tanks with some extra functionality&r, and you can prevent that extra functionality by keeping them disconnected from any networks. "
		""
		"Thus, they are useful in some niche cases where you want to store a small amount of a bunch of different stuff."
	]
	quest.1A6859592E0984D7.quest_subtitle: "i like it"
	quest.1A6859592E0984D7.title: "&bThe Interface&r"
