	quest.5892DD5766B02719.quest_desc: [
		"To get started with &bApplied Energistics 2&r, one must first find a &6meteorite&r that only spawns &6underwater&r (Beach biome). "
		""
		"If you didn't find it, you can craft a &6Meteorite Compass&r, which will point toward the nearest &6Mysterious Cube&r."
		""
		"Once you have found a meteorite, &6mine into its center&r. You will find certus quartz clusters, certus quartz buds, budding certus blocks of various types, and a &bMysterious Cube in the center&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Mine the certus quartz clusters and any certus quartz blocks you find. You can also pick up the budding certus blocks, but without silk touch they will degrade by 1 tier."
		""
		"&6Don't break any flawless budding certus&r, as even with silk touch they will degrade to flawed budding certus, and it is impossible to repair them back to flawless."
		""
		"Also mine the &6Mysterious Cube&r in the center of the meteorite to gain all &64 inscriber presses&r."
	]
	quest.5892DD5766B02719.quest_subtitle: "This is interesting..."
	quest.5892DD5766B02719.title: "&bGetting the initial Materials&r"
	quest.5899110AAC02392C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Advanced Solar Generator&r is a highly upgraded version of the basic &6Solar Generator&r. "
		""
		"It &6produces six times the power&r of its smaller counterpart. It also requires an area of 3x3x3 Blocks in order to be placed. &6Universal Cable&r or other compatible wire can be connected to the side of the base with a green square or the bottom of the Generator. Right-click the generator with a wrench or Configurator set to Rotate to rotate the entire assembly."
		""
		"The &6Advanced Solar Generator only produces full power during a clear day&r. It produces no power during night time, and only 20% of what it would otherwise during a rain."
	]
	quest.5899110AAC02392C.title: "&bAdvanced Solar Generator&r"
